    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="a79c7ab7-d7a3-569d-8d4e-469948ce2885" activityNameId="99f692a4-2fdb-5784-80f4-2fe22d8c2d98" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Phosgene, liquid, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Phosgene, liquid, at plant
The functional unit represent 1 kg of gaseous phosgene. Large uncertainty of the process data due to weak data on the production process and missing data on process emissions.;
CAS number: 000075-44-5; 
Formula: COCl2; 
Synonyms: acid dichloride, Dichlorsäure, carbonyl chloride, Carbonylchlorid; 
UUID: 448a623c-0145-3b9a-925f-33f9e560e585
Raw materials and chemicals used for production, transport of materials to manufacturing plant, estimated emissions to air from production (incomplete), estimation of energy demand and infrastructure of the plant (approximation). Solid wastes omitted.
Location: Data used has no specific geographical origin (stoechiometry). Average europenan processes for raw materials, transport requirements and electricity mix used.
Technology: Production by passing carbon monoxide and cholorine over activated carbon with a yield of 99% (Cl2) rsp. 90% (CO). Inventory bases on stoechiometric calculations. The emissions to air were estimated using mass balance. No process water and therefore no waste water treatment included.
Time period: date of published literature
Production volume: 2.7 Mt worldwide in 1989
Sampling: Process data based on stoechiometric calculations of few literature sources. Energy demand based on approximation from large chemical plant. Process emissions based on estimations only. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_448a623c-0145-3b9a-925f-33f9e560e585.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
